ess in your arm?\n[patient] there\'s some weakness, but nothing too significant.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, any fever or chills?\n[patient] no, none of that.\n[doctor] okay. so, let\'s talk a little bit about your other medical conditions. you\'ve had epilepsy in the past, right?\n[patient] yes.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, have you had any seizures recently?\n[patient] no, not recently. it was a year ago.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, are you still taking any medications for that?\n[patient] yes, i\'m still taking keppra.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, how about your depression?\n[patient] i started therapy last year and i\'m trying to avoid medications for this problem. therapy has been helpful, but i still feel down and stressed.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, have you had any suicidal or homicidal ideations?\n[patient] no, i haven\'t.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, let\'s talk a little bit about your peptic ulcer. so, you had an endoscopy last year?\n[patient] yes, i did.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, what did they find?\n[patient] they found gastritis.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, did you have to take any medications?\n[patient] yes, i had to start protonix.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, have you had any issues with that since then?\n[patient] no, everything has been good.\n[doctor] okay. so, let\'s go ahead and do a quick physical exam. so, i\'m gon na touch your elbow here. does that hurt?\n[patient] yes, it does.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, i\'m gon na touch your elbow here. does that hurt?\n[patient] yes, it does.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, i\'m gon na press on your elbow here. does that hurt?\n[patient] yes, it does.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, i\'m gon na press on your elbow here. does that hurt?\n[patient] yes, it does.\n[doctor] okay. so, i\'m gon na take a look at your elbow. so, i can see some erythema and edema here. and, uh, it\'s warm to the touch. and, uh, it\'s painful to flex and extend. and, uh, i can feel your pulse here. so, let\'s go ahead and look at your x-ray. so, your x-ray of your left arm does not show any evidence of elbow fracture. so, let\'s talk a little bit about my assessment and plan. so, i believe you have left olecranon bursitis caused by repetitive trauma. and, uh, i\'m gon na start you on meloxicam 15 milligrams once daily. i want you to use a pillow to rest your arm on. you can also ice the area. so, do you have any questions about that?\n[patient] no, that sounds good.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, let\'s talk a little bit about your epilepsy. so, it sounds like you\'ve been doing well on keppra and you haven\'t had any seizures recently. so, i\'m gon na continue you on keppra 500 milligrams twice a day. i\'m gon na refill that for you today.\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, let\'s talk a little bit about your depression. so, it sounds like you\'ve been doing well with therapy. and, uh, i\'m gon na start you on lexapro 10 milligrams once daily.\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, let\'s talk a little bit about your peptic ulcer. so, it sounds like you had an endoscopy and they found gastritis. and, uh, you\'ve been doing well on protonix. so, i\'m gon na continue you on protonix 40 milligrams once daily before meals.\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. do you have any questions about that?\n[patient] no, that sounds good.\n[doctor] okay. great. so, do you have any other questions or concerns?\n[patient] no, i think you covered everything.\n[doctor] okay. alright. well, i\'m gon na go ahead and see you out. thanks for coming in today.\n[patient] thanks, doctor. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] hi, anna how are you\n[patient] hey i\'m doing okay, i\'m having some elbow pain\n[doctor] okay, so what\'s going on with your elbow\n[patient] um, i sit at my desk all day for work with my elbows bent and after work it\'s really hard for me to flex and extend my left elbow\n[doctor] okay, and when you say hard, how hard is hard\n[patient] it\'s really stiff and painful\n[doctor] okay, and have you noticed any swelling on the b