LAN\n\nLeft elbow pain.\n• Medical Reasoning: I believe she has left olecranon bursitis caused by repetitive trauma.\n• Medical Treatment: Initiate meloxicam 15 mg once daily.\n• Patient Education and Counseling: I encouraged the patient to use a pillow to rest her arm on. She may also ice the area.\n\nEpilepsy.\n• Medical Reasoning: She has been doing well on Keppra and denies any recent seizures.\n• Medical Treatment: Continue Keppra 500 mg twice a day. This was refilled today.\n\nDepression.\n• Medical Reasoning: She reports doing well with therapy.\n• Medical Treatment: Initiate Lexapro 10 mg once daily.\n\nPeptic ulcer disease.\n• Medical Reasoning: Her recent endoscopy revealed gastritis\n• Medical Treatment: Continue Protonix 40 mg once daily before meals.\n\nPatient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.\n\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] hi, anna, how are you today?\n[patient] i\'m okay, i\'m okay.\n[doctor] alright. so, i know you were here for joint pain. so, tell me a little bit about that. what\'s going on?\n[patient] so, my left elbow\'s been really bothering me.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, how long has it been going on for?\n[patient] it\'s been about a month now.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, what\'s been going on with it?\n[patient] it\'s just been really stiff and painful. and, uh, after i work, it\'s really hard for me to flex and extend my left elbow.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, have you noticed any swelling?\n[patient] yes, i have noticed swelling on the olecranon of my elbow.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, are you right-handed?\n[patient] yes, i am right-handed.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, are you still able to write with your right hand?\n[patient] yes, i can still write, which is great.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, how about typing?\n[patient] typing is really difficult.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, have you noticed any numbness or tingling in your hands?\n[patient] no, i haven\'t.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, any weakness in your arm?\n[patient] there\'s some weakness, but nothing too significant.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, any fever or chills?\n[patient] no, none of that.\n[doctor] okay. so, let\'s talk a little bit about your other medical conditions. you\'ve had epilepsy in the past, right?\n[patient] yes.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, have you had any seizures recently?\n[patient] no, not recently. it was a year ago.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, are you still taking any medications for that?\n[patient] yes, i\'m still taking keppra.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, how about your depression?\n[patient] i started therapy last year and i\'m trying to avoid medications for this problem. therapy has been helpful, but i still feel down and stressed.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, have you had any suicidal or homicidal ideations?\n[patient] no, i haven\'t.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, let\'s talk a little bit about your peptic ulcer. so, you had an endoscopy last year?\n[patient] yes, i did.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, what did they find?\n[patient] they found gastritis.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, did you have to take any medications?\n[patient] yes, i had to start protonix.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, have you had any issues with that since then?\n[patient] no, everything has been good.\n[doctor] okay. so, let\'s go ahead and do a quick physical exam. so, i\'m gon na touch your elbow here. does that hurt?\n[patient] yes, it does.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, i\'m gon na touch your elbow here. does that hurt?\n[patient] yes, it does.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, i\'m gon na press on your elbow here. does that hurt?\n[patient] yes, it does.\n[doctor] okay. and, uh, i\'m gon na press on your elbow here. does that hurt?\n[patient] yes, it does.\n[doctor] okay. so, i\'m gon na take a look at your elbow. so, i can see some erythema and edema here. and, uh, it\'s warm to the touch. and, uh, it\'s painful to flex and extend. and, uh, i can feel your pulse here. so, let\'s go ahead and look at your x-ray.