rior lumbar fusion with hardware in good position.\n\nIMPRESSION\n\nLumbar spine strain.\n\nPLAN\n\nAt this point, I discussed the diagnosis and treatment options with the patient. I have recommended ice and heat. She will continue with Motrin 800 mg 3 times a day with food. She will follow up with me as needed.\n\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] hi, ms. lee, how are you doing today?\n[patient] i\'m doing okay, just a little bit of pain.\n[doctor] okay, so i understand you were at a birthday party and you ran into the railing of the staircase and twisted your back. how are you feeling now?\n[patient] i\'m feeling pretty sore.\n[doctor] mm-hmm. have you had any pain down into your legs?\n[patient] no, just my back.\n[doctor] okay, and does anything make the pain better or worse?\n[patient] lying flat and twisting makes it worse.\n[doctor] okay. have you tried any ibuprofen?\n[patient] i\'ve been taking some ibuprofen.\n[doctor] okay. what kind of ibuprofen have you been taking?\n[patient] just over-the-counter ibuprofen.\n[doctor] okay. have you had any other problems like this before?\n[patient] no, this is the first time.\n[doctor] okay. so let\'s go ahead and go ahead and do a quick physical exam. i\'m gon na check your back. i\'m gon na press on your back here, and it looks like you have a good range of motion without pain. i\'m gon na check your legs, and i\'m gon na straighten your leg up, and that\'s okay. that\'s not painful at all. i\'m gon na check your sensation, and that\'s okay. it feels like you have sensation in your legs. so i\'m gon na take a look at your back x-ray. it looks like you had a lumbar fusion in the past. and you have hardware in your back, and that\'s all in good position. it looks like you have a strain in your back. i\'m gon na give you a diagnosis of lumbar spine strain. so i\'m gon na recommend that you take some ibuprofen 800 milligrams three times a day with food. and i want you to use ice and heat. you can use ice for the first couple of days to try to reduce the pain and swelling. and then you can switch to heat to help loosen up the muscles. if you\'re still having a lot of pain, we can do some physical therapy. and i want you to follow up with me as needed. how does that sound?\n[patient] that sounds good.\n[doctor] okay. do you have any questions?\n[patient] no, that\'s it.\n[doctor] okay. do you have any other medical problems?\n[patient] i have anxiety.\n[doctor] okay. have you been seeing a therapist for that?\n[patient] no, i haven\'t.\n[doctor] okay. i\'m gon na refer you to a therapist. i think that would be helpful. i\'m gon na order some physical therapy and some physical therapy exercises for you to do at home. and i\'m gon na give you a prescription for some ibuprofen. and if you\'re still having a lot of pain, we can do some injections. does that sound okay?\n[patient] yes, that sounds good.\n[doctor] okay. i\'m gon na have my nurse come in and get you checked out.\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] hi, ms. lee. how are you doing today?\n[patient] i\'m doing okay. i\'m still having some back pain. but i\'m really glad to be here.\n[doctor] yeah, i\'m glad to see you too. um, so i know you\'ve had a pretty rough couple of days. um, can you tell me a little bit about what happened?\n[patient] so, i was at a birthday party, and i was running up the stairs, and i ran into the railing, and i twisted my back, and i\'ve been in a lot of pain ever since.\n[doctor] okay. and where exactly did you hit your back?\n[patient] so, um, i hit it right in the lower back, like, like the lumbar area.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any pain radiating down your legs?\n[patient] no, not really.\n[doctor] okay. and when you, when you, when you ran into the railing, did you feel a snap or a pop at all?\n[patient] no, i did not.\n[doctor] okay. and do you feel like you\'re able to move your back around at all?\n[patient] not really. it\'s really sore. and when i lie down, it hurts a little bit more. and when i twist it, it hurts a lot more.\n[doctor] okay. and how would you rate your pain on a scale of one to ten?\n[patient] probably a seven.\n[doctor] okay. and have you been taking any medication for the pain?\n[patient] i\'ve been taking ibuprofen. i took a few ibuprofen last night.\n[doctor] okay. and when was the last time you took some?\n[patient] um, i think it was last night. i took a few.\n[doctor] okay. and have you tried using ice and heat?\n[patient] i\'ve tried using ice. i haven\'t tried using heat.\n[doctor] okay. and how long have you been experiencing this pain for?\n[patient] i\'ve been experiencing it since last night.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any other medical problems?\n[patient] i have anxiety.\n[doctor] okay. and have you had any surgeries?\n[patient] i had a lumbar fusion.\n[doctor] okay. and when was that?\n[patient] i think it was about six years ago.\n[doctor] okay. and did you have any hardware put in?\n[patient] yeah, i did.\n[doctor] okay. and is the hardware still in?\n[patient] yes, it is.\n[doctor] okay. and is it still working okay?\n[patient] yeah, it is.\n[doctor] okay. well, let\'s go ahead and do a quick physical exam. i\'m gon na check your back. does that hurt when i push on it?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any numbness or tingling in your legs?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and when i bend you forward, does it hurt?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and when i straighten you back up, does it hurt?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and when i push on your back, does it hurt?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and can you move your back around?\n[patient] yes.\n[doctor] okay. and does it hurt when you move?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and are you able to straighten your legs out?\n[patient] yes.\n[doctor] okay. and are you able to bend them?\n[patient] yes.\n[doctor] okay. and when you bend them, does it hurt?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and when you straighten them out, does it hurt?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any numbness or tingling in your legs?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any weakness in your legs?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. all right. let\'s go ahead and look at your x-rays. and your x-rays show that you had a lumbar fusion in the past. and the hardware is in good position. and, um, you don\'t have any signs of a fracture right now. so, um, based on your history and your physical exam, i think you have a lumbar strain. and i\'m gon na prescribe you some ibuprofen, 800 milligrams three times a day with food. and i want you to use ice and heat. i don\'t want you to use heat at first. i want you to use ice for the first couple of days. and then i want you to switch over to heat. and i want you to take your ibuprofen three times a day with food. and if your pain doesn\'t get better, then we\'re gon na need to do some further testing. but i don\'t think that\'s necessary at this point. is that okay?\n[patient] yeah, that sounds good. thank you.\n[doctor] okay. is there anything else i can do for you?\n[patient] no, that\'s it.\n[doctor] okay. all right. take care.\n[patient] thank you. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Reference Answer:\n[doctor] hello mrs. lee , i see you\'re here for back pain .\n[patient] yes .\n[doctor] hey dragon , i\'m seeing mrs. lee today for , uh , back pain . she\'s a 40-year-old female . so can you tell me what happened to you ?\n[patient] yes . i was at a birthday party and it was surprise party . so we were all like crunched behind and hiding . and when the person came in we all jumped out , and then i fell down the little stair and i rammed my back into the railing of the s- , uh , staircase .\n[doctor] so it was a surprise for you too ?\n[patient] yes it was .\n[doctor] very good . okay . so , um , did it hurt because you hit it , or did you twist ? what happened when you ?\n[patient] i think it was my motion-\n[doctor] okay .\n[pa