e fevers\n[doctor] okay and how about your bowels are you having any abdominal pain or diarrhea\n[patient] no i\'m not having any abdominal pain or diarrhea\n[doctor] okay and so i\'m gon na go ahead and do a quick physical exam\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] so on exam of your abdomen i do appreciate some warmth to palpation but it\'s not tender to palpation and there\'s no evidence of cellulitis on your skin exam i do appreciate some swelling and pain to palpation of your elbow joints bilaterally and i do see a small bullseye rash on your left abdominal quadrant\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] all right so let\'s talk about the results of your labs so your wbc was within normal limits all of your other labs were normal as well but your lyme titer was elevated\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] so i\'m gon na go ahead and prescribe doxycycline one hundred milligrams twice a day for three weeks i\'m gon na touch base with an infectious disease doctor to ensure that nothing else needs to be done and i\'d like to see you back in a week for follow-up for this\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] so for your hypertension i\'m gon na go ahead and order a lipid panel and you can continue to take lisinopril ten milligrams a day and i\'ve refilled that for you\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] and for your diabetes type two i\'m gon na go ahead and order a hemoglobin a1c to ensure that no medication changes are needed and you can continue to take your metformin\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] and any questions for me\n[patient] no i think that\'s it\n[doctor] okay all right well i\'ll see you in a week }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Reference Answer:\n[doctor] we\'re gon na go right to the front- . so when you touch that- hi , michelle , how are you ?\n[patient] i\'m good . how are you ?\n[doctor] i\'m good . so i know the nurse told you about dax . i\'d like to dax a little bit about you , okay ?\n[patient] okay .\n[doctor] all right . so , michelle is a 31-year-old female with a past medical history of type 2 diabetes and hyper