 her high blood sugar is not an issue.\n\nThe patient denies any fever or chills. She denies chest pain or shortness of breath. She denies abdominal pain or burning when she urinates. She denies joint pain or muscle aches.\n\nShe notes that she has osteoarthritis, and that nothing seems out of the ordinary for her joint pain.\n\nThe patient has a history of atrial fibrillation. She states that she has felt her heart racing when she is anxious; however, other than that, she has not experienced any issues. She is currently taking metoprolol 25 mg 2 times per day.\n\nRegarding her acid reflux, she states that she has been doing well. She has been taking the medication that was prescribed to her, and it has been very helpful. She is on the Protonix 40 mg once daily, and she is doing well with that\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n\n• Constitutional: Negative for fever, chills\n• Cardiovascular: Negative for chest pain\n• Respiratory: Negative for shortness of breath.\n• Gastrointestinal: Negative for abdominal pain.\n• Genitourinary: No dysuria.\n• Musculoskeletal: No Arthralgias, Myalgias.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAMINATION\n\nConstitutional\n• General Appearance: appear in no distress.\n\nNeck\n• General Examination: Her thyroid is a little enlarged but nontender. There are no carotid bruits. Respiratory\n• Auscultation of Lungs: Clear bilaterally. Cardiovascular\n• Auscultation of Heart: Irregular rate and rhythm. Musculoskeletal\n• Examination of Abdomen: Nice soft and have no edema in lower extremities.\n\nRESULTS\n\nGlucose: elevated.\nHbA1c: elevated.\n\nASSESSMENT AND PLAN\n\nMs. Hannah Phillips is a 52-year-old female who presents for evaluation of high blood sugar.\n\nDiabetes.\n• Medical Reasoning: Elevated blood glucose and hemoglobin A1c levels based on recent labs.\n• Additional Testing: We will order a complete metabolic panel for further evaluation.\n• Medical Treatment: Initiate metformin 500 mg twice daily. Encouraged dietary modifications. The patient will be given a glucometer to monitor her glucose levels at home.\n\nAtrial Fibrillation.\n\n• Medical Reasoning: Asymptomatic and well-controlled at this time.\n• Medical Treatment: Continue metoprolol 25 mg twice daily. Refilled today.\n\nHistory of Reflux.\n\n• Medical Reasoning: Well-controlled on current regimen.\n• Medical Treatment: Continue Protonix 40 mg daily.\n\nPatient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.\n\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] hi, ms. phillips, how are you?\n[patient] i\'m okay. i\'m just feeling really lightheaded and i was seeing spots in my vision and i was really dizzy. so, i went to the emergency room and they told me that my blood sugar was really high.\n[doctor] mm-hmm, okay. and what was going on that day? were you eating something different?\n[patient] i think i just ate too many sweets during the holidays.\n[doctor] mm-hmm, okay. and then you went to the emergency room. what did they do for you there?\n[patient] they gave me iv fluids and they told me to get into a routine and watch my diet.\n[doctor] okay. and how are you feeling now?\n[patient] i\'m feeling a little better, but i\'m still having trouble getting back into my routine and i\'m staying with family during the holidays and it\'s hard to stick to my diet.\n[doctor] okay. so, have you noticed any fever or chills?\n[patient] no, i haven\'t.\n[doctor] okay. any chest pain or shortness of breath?\n[patient] no, nothing like that.\n[doctor] okay. any abdominal pain or burning when you urinate?\n[patient] no, nothing like that.\n[doctor] okay. any joint pain or muscle aches?\n[patient] no, nothing seems out of the ordinary for my joint pain.\n[doctor] okay. and how about your heart? have you noticed anything unusual with that?\n[patient] i have atrial fibrillation. i feel like my heart racing when i\'m anxious, but other than that, i have not had any issues.\n[doctor] okay. and you\'re currently taking metoprolol 25 mg twice a day?\n[patient] yes, i am.\n[doctor] okay. and how about your acid reflux? how\'s that been?\n[patient] i\'ve been doing well. i\'ve been taking the medication that was prescribed to me and it\'s been very helpful.\n[doctor] okay. and you\'re on protonix 40 mg once a day?\n[patient] yes, i am.\n[doctor] okay. and how has that been?\n[patient] it\'s been really good.\n[doctor] okay. let\'s go ahead and go through a quick physical exam. i\'m just gon na check your vitals and do a quick exam. so, your blood pressure is 130 over 70, your heart rate is 90, and your respiratory rate is 16. let\'s go ahead and listen to your heart and lungs. your heart sounds irregular, but otherwise, it sounds nice and clear. your lungs are clear bilaterally. i\'m gon na go ahead and check your abdomen. your abdomen is nice and soft. i\'m not feeling any masses or any tenderness there. i\'m gon na check your thyroid. it\'s a little bit enlarged, but it\'s not tender. i\'m not hearing any carotid bruits. your heart is irregular, but otherwise, your physical exam is normal. let\'s go ahead and look at your labs. your glucose was elevated, and your hemoglobin a1c was elevated as well. so, let\'s talk a little bit about your diabetes. i think you have diabetes, and i\'m gon na go ahead and order a complete metabolic panel for further evaluation. we\'re gon na initiate metformin 500 mg twice a day. we\'re gon na encourage dietary modifications, and we\'re gon na give you a glucometer to monitor your glucose levels at home. let\'s talk about your atrial fibrillation. it sounds like you\'re doing well. you\'re currently on metoprolol 25 mg twice a day. i\'m gon na go ahead and refill that for you today. and then for your reflux, you\'re doing well. you\'re on protonix 40 mg a day. i\'m gon na continue that for you. does that sound good?\n[patient] that sounds good.\n[doctor] okay. is there anything else that you\'d like to ask or discuss?\n[patient] no, that\'s it.\n[doctor] okay