ient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.\n\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] good morning, janet how are you?\n[patient] i\'m doing okay, how are you?\n[doctor] i\'m doing well. so, janet, i understand you\'re here for some joint pain. can you tell me a little bit more about that?\n[patient] yes, i\'ve been having some pain in my knees.\n[doctor] okay. and where is the pain located?\n[patient] it\'s in both of my knees.\n[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any swelling in your legs or any pins and needles in your feet?\n[patient] no, no swelling and no pins and needles.\n[doctor] okay. have you had any fever or chills?\n[patient] no, no fever or chills.\n[doctor] okay. and have you had any nausea or vomiting?\n[patient] no, no nausea or vomiting.\n[doctor] okay. have you had any chest pain or shortness of breath?\n[patient] no, no chest pain or shortness of breath.\n[doctor] okay. have you had any injuries to your knees or any trauma to your knees?\n[patient] i\'ve been doing stair workouts, i thought it was building muscle on my knees.\n[doctor] okay. and you\'ve been doing stair workouts?\n[patient] yes, stair workouts.\n[doctor] okay. and have you had any injuries to your knees before?\n[patient] no, none.\n[doctor] okay. have you had any other surgeries?\n[patient] yes, i had a right shoulder rotator cuff repair about two years ago.\n[doctor] okay. and have you had any problems since that point?\n[patient] no, none.\n[doctor] okay. are your diabetes well-controlled?\n[patient] yes, they are well-controlled.\n[doctor] okay. do you have high blood pressure?\n[patient] yes, i do.\n[doctor] okay. how do you manage that?\n[patient] i monitor it and i take norvasc five milligrams a day.\n[doctor] okay. and have you noticed that your blood pressure has been elevated since your joint pain started?\n[patient] no, it has not.\n[doctor] okay. have you had any other symptoms?\n[patient] no