te. so, your blood pressure is running a little high, but your heart and lungs sound normal. there\'s no edema in your legs or feet. and your abdomen is nice and soft. so, let\'s talk a little bit more about your diet. i know you mentioned you\'re trying to reduce your sodium intake. have you been following the dash diet?\n[patient] no, i have not.\n[doctor] okay. and i know you\'ve been monitoring your salt intake, but how much are you taking in a day?\n[patient] i\'m not sure.\n[doctor] okay. so, the dash diet is a diet that\'s really good for people with high blood pressure. it\'s a diet that\'s low in sodium and high in potassium. and it\'s also high in fiber. so, i\'m gon na give you some materials on that. and i want you to try to keep your sodium intake below 1500 to 2000 milligrams per day. so, let\'s talk a little bit about your medications. i know you\'re on the benicar and the amlodipine. have you noticed any side effects from those?\n[patient] no, i haven\'t.\n[doctor] okay. and i\'m gon na go ahead and add one more medication to your regimen. this is called spironolactone. it\'s a medication that\'s gon na help lower your blood pressure. it\'s gon na increase your potassium levels a little bit. so, i want you to be careful with your diet. try to eat foods that are high in potassium. i\'m gon na give you a list of those. i want you to check your blood pressure and potassium levels in two weeks. and if we\'re not seeing any improvement in your blood pressure, we may need to add another medication. but let\'s try this first. so, i\'m gon na prescribe you 100 milligrams of spironolactone once a day. and i want you to start that today. so, do you have any questions about that?\n[patient] no, i don\'t think so.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any questions about the dash diet?\n[patient] no, i don\'t think so.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any other questions?\n[patient] no, i don\'t think so.\n[doctor] okay. so, let\'s go ahead and schedule you for a follow up in two weeks. we\'ll check your blood pressure and your potassium levels. and i\'ll see how you\'re doing. and if we need to make any changes, we will. okay?\n[patient] okay, that sounds good.\n[doctor] okay. and i\'m gon na give you some materials on the dash diet. i want you to access the american heart association website. they have a lot of information on it. and i want you to meet 30 minutes of walking most days. okay?\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. and i want you to reduce your sodium intake to 1500 to 2000 milligrams per day. okay?\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. and i\'ll see you in two weeks. bye.\n[patient] bye.\n[doctor] hey, jordan, how are you?\n[patient] i\'m doing well, thank you.\n[doctor] good. i\'m glad to hear that. so, i understand you\'re here today for some palpitations and high blood pressure. what\'s going on?\n[patient] yeah, i\'ve been having a lot of palpitations and my blood pressure has been really high.\n[doctor] okay. and when did this start?\n[patient] it started in march.\n[doctor] and did you have to go to the emergency room for it?\n[patient] yeah, i did.\n[doctor] okay. and what did they do for you?\n[patient] they just checked me out. they said it was a panic attack.\n[doctor] okay. and have you had any other episodes since then?\n[patient] no, i have not.\n[doctor] okay. and are you taking any medications for your blood pressure?\n[patient] yes, i am.\n[doctor] okay. what medications are you taking?\n[patient] i\'m on benicar and amlodipine.\n[doctor] okay. and how long have you been on those?\n[patient] about a month now.\n[doctor] okay. and are you taking them as directed?\n[patient] yeah, i am.\n[doctor] okay. and have you been monitoring your blood pressure at home?\n[patient] yes, i have.\n[doctor] okay. and what are your blood pressure readings?\n[\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] hi, jordan, how are you?\n[patient] i\'m doing alright. i\'ve been feeling a little anxious and my blood pressure\'s been running a little