sure\'s been running a little high.\n[doctor] okay. so i see here that you were in the emergency room in march for palpitations and hypertension. is that correct?\n[patient] yeah, that\'s right.\n[doctor] and did you have any other episodes of palpitations?\n[patient] no, not since then.\n[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any other symptoms since then?\n[patient] no, not really.\n[doctor] okay. and how\'s your blood pressure been?\n[patient] it\'s been running a little high. i\'ve been checking it at home, it\'s been running between 146 and 155.\n[doctor] okay. and have you been taking your medications?\n[patient] i\'ve been taking them, but i haven\'t been checking my blood pressure as regularly as i should.\n[doctor] okay. and who\'s your primary care physician?\n[patient] dr. smith.\n[doctor] okay. and what medications is she having you on?\n[patient] she put me on benicar hct and amlodipine.\n[doctor] okay. and how long have you been on those?\n[patient] since march.\n[doctor] okay. and how are you feeling?\n[patient] i\'m feeling good. i\'m just feeling a little anxious and my blood pressure\'s been running a little high.\n[doctor] okay. and are you doing anything to help with your blood pressure?\n[patient] i\'ve been trying to reduce my salt intake.\n[doctor] okay. and how\'s that going?\n[patient] it\'s been going good. i\'ve been watching what i eat and i\'ve been walking on the treadmill a lot.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any family history of hypertension?\n[patient] yes, my mother has it.\n[doctor] okay. and how old was she when she was diagnosed?\n[patient] she was diagnosed when she was in her early 50s.\n[doctor] okay. and has she been on any medications for that?\n[patient] yes, she\'s been on medications for it.\n[doctor] okay. and how\'s she doing?\n[patient] she\'s doing alright.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any other medical problems?\n[patient] i\'ve been having some problems with my thyroid.\n[doctor] okay. and when was that diagnosed?