t ate fried chicken today, and it made me really sick.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, how many times a day do you eat?\n[patient] i eat like three times a day.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, do you drink a lot of fluids?\n[patient] yeah, i drink a lot of fluids. i drink soda. i drink water. i drink juice.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, have you noticed any blood in your stool?\n[patient] no, i have not.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, have you noticed any weight loss?\n[patient] no, i haven\'t.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, how are you sleeping at night?\n[patient] i\'m not sleeping very well. i\'m having a lot of trouble sleeping.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, have you been having any stress?\n[patient] i\'ve been having a lot of stress. i\'ve been working a lot. i\'ve been going to school. i\'ve been trying to do a lot of things.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, have you been feeling stressed for a long time?\n[patient] yeah, i\'ve been feeling stressed for a long time. it\'s just been really bad lately.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, have you tried any stress relief techniques?\n[patient] um, i\'ve been trying to take some deep breaths. i\'ve been trying to relax. i\'ve been trying to take some baths. i\'ve been trying to do some yoga.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, do you have any other medical problems?\n[patient] no, i don\'t.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, do you have any allergies to any medications?\n[patient] no, i don\'t think so.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, have you taken any medications in the past?\n[patient] no, i haven\'t.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, have you been to the emergency room for this?\n[patient] no, i haven\'t. i\'ve been trying to avoid going.\n[doctor] okay. well, i\'m gon na go ahead and examine you. and, um, everything looks good. your abdomen is soft, non-tender. you do have some gas and bloating, but your bowels are moving well. and, um, your lungs are clear. your heart is regular. so, um, i\'m gon na go ahead and tell you what i think is going on. i think you have irritable bowel syndrome. and it\'