[92mlitellm.acompletion(model='gpt-4o', api_base=None, messages=[{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You are a fair judge assistant assigned to deliver insightful feedback that compares individual performances, highlighting how each stands relative to others within the same cohort.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of two responses strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, choose a better response between Response A and Response B. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: "(write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (A or B)"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###Instruction:\n\nImagine you are a medical professional tasked with evaluating simulated doctor-patient conversations generated from summary notes. \nThese conversations should accurately reconstruct interactions based on the SOAP (Subjective, Objective, Assessment, Plan) format provided in the notes.\n\nHere is the medical note:\n#############################\nCHIEF COMPLAINT\n\nFollow up irritable bowel syndrome (IBS).\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS\n\nMs. Brittany Edwards is a pleasant 32-year-old female who returns in follow up for irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) with functional abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting.\n\nMs. Edwards was last seen in August 2019 with flares of abdominal pain and was diagnosed with irritable bowel syndrome that was treated with Bentyl. She had a previous prescription for Reglan that she received from the emergency room that she used as needed for nausea. She was instructed to start a low dose fiber supplement such as Citrucel daily, probiotics to help with gas and bloating, and Bentyl up to 4 times daily for intestinal cramping. She was instructed to discontinue Reglan and to use Zofran as needed for nausea. Neuromodulators such as Elavil and Buspar were discussed but not started.\n\nMs. Edwards continues to have intermittent abdominal symptoms. Monday through Thursday she has less flare ups of her symptoms but states she is currently having cramps and sharp pains. She describes she recently ate shrimp which caused her to have both upper and lower abdominal pain and bloating. However, she notices episodes of diarrhea after eating chicken alfredo and consuming alcohol. She does not believe the alfredo contributes to her symptoms. The patient states she consumes 2 drinks when out of either tequila or brown liquor and occasionally a martini. She does her best to avoid “heavy foods,” but ate fried chicken today without any symptoms. She has stopped drinking sodas which has been helpful.\u202fThe patient reports passing 2-3 formed stools a day.\n\nREVIEW OF SYMPTOMS\n\n•\u202fGastrointestinal:\u202fPositive nausea, diarrhea, and abdominal pain.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAM\n\nAlert and cooperative, appears stated age.\n\nRespiratory\nLungs clear to auscultation bilaterally.\n\nCardiovascular\nHeart regular rate and rhythm.\n\nGastrointestinal\nAbdomen soft, non-tender, no masses or organomegaly. Normoactive bowel sounds.\n\nASSESSMENT\n\n• Irritable bowel syndrome\n\nBrittany Edwards is a 32-year-old established patient who returned today to discuss management of IBS and functional abdominal pain made worse by high stress, poor eating habits, and poor sleeping habits.\n\nPLAN\n\nI have encouraged dietary and lifestyle modifications as well as starting a neuromodulator, such as Elavil 25 mg at bedtime for IBS. She can use\u202fBentyl\u202f20 mg as needed 30-45 minutes\u202fbefore eating out at a restaurant. She can also use Zofran as needed for nausea. However, I have encouraged her to reduce greasy fatty foods and alcohol consumption.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\nSend MyChart message in 1 month regarding any side effects of issues with Elavil or if dose adjustments are needed.\nReturn to clinic in 1 month or sooner if needed.\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] good morning how are you\n[patient] good morning doctor\n[doctor] hey good morning so i see that you\'re here for follow up for your irritable bowel syndrome or ibs what\'s going on for you\n[patient] so i\'ve been having a lot of abdominal pain and nausea and vomiting\n[doctor] okay and when did this start\n[patient] it\'s been going on for a while now\n[doctor] okay so this is new or has this been going on for a while\n[patient] it\'s been going on for a while\n[doctor] okay and when was the last time you were in\n[patient] i think i was in august\n[doctor] okay and what did we do for you last time\n[patient] i think you gave me bentyl\n[doctor] okay and i also gave you a prescription for reglan\n[patient] yeah\n[doctor] okay and what did you do with that\n[patient] i used it as needed for nausea\n[doctor] okay and then i also told you to start a low dose fiber supplement such as citrucel daily and probiotics to help with gas and bloating and to take bentyl up to four times a day for intestinal cramping\n[patient] yeah\n[doctor] and i also told you to discontinue the reglan and to use zofran as needed for nausea\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] and i know we discussed neuromodulators like elavil and buspar but we didn\'t start those yet\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] okay so tell me a little bit more about what\'s been going on since then\n[patient] so i\'ve been having a lot of flares of abdominal pain and i\'ve been taking the bentyl as needed and the citrucel and i\'ve been trying to do the probiotics but i haven\'t been doing it consistently\n[doctor] okay and how often are you having these flares\n[patient] i would say maybe monday through thursday i\'m okay but then on friday i\'m having a lot of cramps and sharp pains\n[doctor] okay and anything that makes it better or worse\n[patient] yeah i had shrimp the other day and i had upper and lower abdominal pain and a lot of bloating\n[doctor] okay and did that happen after the shrimp or was it before\n[patient] it was after\n[doctor] okay and what else has been going on\n[patient] i had chicken alfredo and that makes me have diarrhea\n[doctor] okay and does that happen every time you have chicken alfredo\n[patient] pretty much yeah\n[doctor] okay and any other foods that make you have diarrhea\n[patient] yeah i drink two drinks when i\'m out and i have a martini occasionally and i do my best to avoid heavy foods but i had fried chicken today and i didn\'t have any symptoms\n[doctor] okay and how about sodas have you been drinking those\n[patient] i stopped drinking those\n[doctor] okay and that\'s been helpful\n[patient] yeah\n[doctor] okay and how about your bowel movements how often are you passing stool\n[patient] i\'m passing 2 to 3 formed stools a day\n[doctor] okay and are they loose or are they hard\n[patient] they\'re kind of loose\n[doctor] okay all right so let\'s do a quick physical exam on you\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] hey so i\'m gon na press on your belly here and i\'m gon na listen to your heart and lungs\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] hey so your heart sounds good and your lungs sound good\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] hey so your belly is soft and non tender no masses or organomegaly and your bowel sounds are normal\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] hey so based on your symptoms i think you\'re doing okay but we need to make a few adjustments so i\'m gon na prescribe you elavil 25 milligrams at bedtime for your ibs\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] and you can take bentyl 20 milligrams 30 to 45 minutes before eating out at a restaurant and you can use zofran as needed for nausea\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] and i think we need to reduce your greasy fatty foods and your alcohol consumption\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] and i know we talked about elavil and buspar before but we\'re gon na start with the elavil first\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] hey so i want you to send me a mychart message in one month regarding any side effects or if you need any dose adjustments and we\'ll see you back in one month or sooner if needed\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] hey do you have any questions for me\n[patient] no\n[doctor] okay alrighty hey take care\n[patient] thanks }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] hi, brittany. it\'s good to see you. how are you doing?\n[patient] i\'m doing okay. i\'m just having some stomach issues.\n[doctor] okay. so, i\'m gon na go ahead and review your vitals. your blood pressure is a little bit high, but that\'s okay. it\'s not concerning for today. i\'m gon na go ahead and review your symptoms. so, you\'re having some stomach issues. you\'re having some nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain. and when was this started?\n[patient] um, i think it started about a week ago.\n[doctor] okay. and have you had this before?\n[patient] yeah, i have. i\'ve had it a lot in the past, but it seems to be getting worse.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, what makes it better? what makes it worse?\n[patient] um, i think it\'s just stress. i think it\'s just stress. and, um, i think i might be eating some bad foods, but i don\'t know.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, what kind of foods are you eating?\n[patient] i don\'t know. i just eat a lot of greasy foods, i guess. and, um, i have been drinking a lot of soda, which i know i shouldn\'t be. i\'ve been trying to cut back on that, but it\'s hard.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, what kind of greasy foods?\n[patient] um, like fried chicken. i love fried chicken.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, do you have any other symptoms?\n[patient] i have some diarrhea, and i have some abdominal pain. and i feel really bloated.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, have you noticed any other symptoms?\n[patient] no, that\'s it. i\'ve been feeling really nauseous.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, what have you been eating that makes you nauseous?\n[patient] um, i think it\'s the fried chicken. i jus