k we can try to get you back on the medicine. and i\'m going to lower the dose of the lisinopril to 10 milligrams a day. we\'ll try that and see how you do. i think it\'s important to get you off the hydrochlorothiazide because it\'s causing some side effects. we can try to get you off that. and then we can try to get you back on the lisinopril. i know you were checking your blood pressure at home. are you checking it in the morning and in the evening?\n[patient] yeah, i\'m checking it in the morning and in the evening.\n[doctor] okay. and are you finding that it\'s higher in the evening?\n[patient] yes, it\'s higher in the evening.\n[doctor] okay. well, it\'s not uncommon for blood pressure to be higher at night. but it\'s good that you\'re checking it and we can try to get you back on the medicine. and i know that you have been drinking a lot of alcohol. have you been drinking at all?\n[patient] yeah, i drink about 4 to 5 times a week.\n[doctor] okay. and how much are you drinking each time?\n[patient] i\'m not sure.\n[doctor] okay. well, let\'s just say it\'s a lot. and i know that you\'re interested in getting off the alcohol. and i think if you could stop drinking, your blood pressure would probably be a lot better. have you thought about that?\n[patient] yeah, i have.\n[doctor] okay. well, let\'s talk a little bit about the naltrexone. i know you were interested in that. i\'m going to start you on that. we\'ll do the injectable form. and we\'ll start you on that on may 17th. and we\'ll do it every week. and we\'ll see how you do. and i think it will help you cut back on the drinking. are you okay with that?\n[patient] yeah, i\'m okay with that.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any questions about the naltrexone?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. well, i\'m going to prescribe you the naltrexone. and we\'ll start you on it next week. and we\'ll see how you do. and i think it will really help you. so let\'s talk a little bit about your other medical history. you have