had any fever or chills?\n[patient] no, no fever or chills.\n[doctor] okay. and what\'s going on with your sexual activity? are you having any issues with that?\n[patient] well, i just recently found out that my partner has been having other partners for a while.\n[doctor] okay. and how long have you been with this partner?\n[patient] we\'ve been together for about three years.\n[doctor] okay. and how long have you known that he\'s been having other partners?\n[patient] recently. he told me.\n[doctor] okay. and how recently did he tell you?\n[patient] i think it was last week.\n[doctor] okay. and how did that make you feel?\n[patient] it was really upsetting.\n[doctor] yeah, i can imagine. that would be really upsetting. and so, you\'re here because you\'re concerned about stds?\n[patient] yeah, i want to get checked out.\n[doctor] okay. and have you had any stds in the past?\n[patient] no, i have not.\n[doctor] okay. and have you had any abnormal pap smears?\n[patient] yes, i had an abnormal pap about ten years ago.\n[doctor] okay. and what happened with that?\n[patient] i had to get it repeated and it was normal after that.\n[doctor] okay. and have you had any pap smears since then?\n[patient] yes, i have.\n[doctor] and were they all normal?\n[patient] yes, they have been.\n[doctor] okay. and when was the last one?\n[patient] about six months ago.\n[doctor] okay. and was that normal?\n[patient] yes, it was normal.\n[doctor] okay. and how long have you been sexually active with this partner?\n[patient] we\'ve been together for three years.\n[doctor] okay. and do you use any form of birth control?\n[patient] no, we do not.\n[doctor] okay. and do you use condoms?\n[patient] no, we do not.\n[doctor] okay. so, let\'s go ahead and do a quick physical exam. i\'m gon na do a pelvic exam. and i\'m gon na check for any external lesions or any abnormalities. i\'ll also check your cervix and your vaginal walls. okay?\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. i\'ll be gentle. i\'ll just touch your abdomen and then i\'ll do a pelvic exam. okay?\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. everything looks normal here. no external lesions, normal labia majora and labia minora. normal physiological discharge with normal color and odor. your cervix is normal, your vaginal wall is normal. no cervical motion tenderness or masses noted. i\'ll just take some swabs of your cervix and vaginal walls. these are gon na be sent for std testing. we\'ll test for gonorrhea, chlamydia, trichomoniasis, syphilis, hiv, and hepatitis c. we\'ll call you with the results.\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. do you have any other questions or concerns?\n[patient] no, that\'s it.\n[doctor] okay. i\'ll have my nurse come in and help you get dressed. she\'ll also be able to answer any other questions you may have. and we\'ll have the results back in a few days. do you have any other health insurance or any other providers that you see?\n[patient] no, i just have my primary care doctor.\n[doctor] okay. okay. and do you have a mychart account?\n[patient] no, i do not.\n[doctor] okay. we\'ll be able to get the results to you through the mail or you can come back and pick them up. okay?\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. thank you. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] hi, ms. ross, it\'s nice to meet you. i\'m doctor john.\n[patient] hi, doctor john. nice to meet you too.\n[doctor] so, you know, i know you\'re here for a full-spectrum std test. is that correct?\n[patient] yes, that\'s correct.\n[doctor] okay. so, you know, i\'m gon na go ahead and review your vitals. so, you\'re twenty-three years old. your last name is ross. your date of birth is may fifth, nineteen ninety-seven. your last place of residence is in the united states. your address is in charlotte, north carolina. your last place of employment is a bank.\n[patient] yes, that\'s correct.\n[doctor] okay. so, you know, i know that you\'re here for a full-spectrum std test. can you tell me a little bit more about what\'s going