bout your medical history. do you have any medical problems?\n[patient] i have type two diabetes.\n[doctor] okay. and how are you managing that?\n[patient] i\'m managing it with diet and exercise.\n[doctor] okay. and any other medical problems?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. any surgeries?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and any allergies?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and any medications?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. so, i\'m gon na go ahead and review some of the results from the ultrasound. so, the ultrasound does show that you have multiple gallstones present in your gallbladder. and i do appreciate some mild thickening. but your common bile duct size is within normal limits at four point one millimeters. so, it looks like you have some mild cholecystitis with gallstones. and i do not appreciate any frank obstruction. but it does look like your gallbladder is inflamed. and this has probably happened over the last few weeks or since you\'ve been symptomatic. so, i do think you need some surgical intervention. i think you need a laparoscopic cholecystectomy. so, i\'m gon na go ahead and order that for you. and i\'m gon na schedule you for next week. and i\'m gon na have my nurse come in and we\'ll go over the preoperative, intraoperative, and postoperative course of care. and then we\'ll get you scheduled for surgery.\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. so, i know this is a big surgery. but this is something that\'s going to resolve your symptoms. and we\'ll get you back on your feet and hiking again in no time. okay?\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. so, i\'m gon na have my nurse come in and we\'ll go over all the details. and then we\'ll get you scheduled for surgery. so, do you have any questions for me?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. all right. so, i\'m gon na have my nurse come in and we\'ll get you scheduled for surgery. and then we\'ll get you on the road to recovery.\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. all right. so, i\'m gon na have my nurse come in and we\'ll