od?\n[patient] yes, it does.\n[doctor] okay. i\'m going to have my nurse come in and get you checked in and get you set up with your prescriptions and everything. do you have any questions?\n[patient] no, i think that\'s it.\n[doctor] okay. great. i\'ll see you in about 20 minutes. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] hi, matthew. how are you?\n[patient] i\'m doing okay. i\'m doing okay.\n[doctor] all right. so you\'re here today for right shoulder pain. how did this happen?\n[patient] i was playing football, playing pick up football and i got tackled a couple of times and i landed on my right shoulder and i\'ve been having pain since then.\n[doctor] okay. and were you able to continue playing after that?\n[patient] i was able to continue playing, but i\'ve been having pain since then.\n[doctor] okay. and where is the pain located?\n[patient] it\'s located on the back of my shoulder.\n[doctor] okay. and are you feeling any numbness or tingling in your fingers?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and have you lost any strength in your hand?\n[patient] no, my hand\'s okay, but i\'ve been trying to avoid lifting anything heavy.\n[doctor] okay. and can you touch your shoulder to your ear?\n[patient] no, i can\'t because of the pain.\n[doctor] okay. and are you having any problems with your neck?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and have you had any previous injuries to your right shoulder?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and have you had a fever or chills?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and did you hit your head at all?\n[patient] yes, i hit my head, but i didn\'t pass out.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any other medical problems?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. all right. so let\'s go ahead and do a quick physical exam. so on your neck exam, i\'m not finding any tenderness to palpation. full range of motion. on your head, there does not appear to be any trauma, no ecchymosis or bruising. on your examination of your right shoulder, i do appreciate pain to palpation of t