ht arm while you\'re awake to provide a little bit more support. i\'m gon na have you ice your elbow for twenty minutes, three times a day. you can take ibuprofen six hundred milligrams every six hours with food. and that\'s gon na be for a week. i\'m gon na have you hold off on creating pottery for the next two weeks to allow your arm to heal. if you continue to have elbow pain, we may consider formal physical therapy at your next visit. i\'m gon na encourage you to check and record your blood sugars every day. i\'m gon na increase your metformin to one thousand milligrams twice a day. you\'re gon na continue to take your lisinopril. you\'re gon na continue with your walking routine. i\'m gon na order a hemoglobin a1c test to get a more accurate assessment of your long-term blood sugar levels. and i\'m gon na encourage you to continue with your regular blood sugar checks. i\'m gon na have you come back and see me in two weeks to review the results of the hemoglobin a1c test and discuss your progress. and if you have any other questions, feel free to ask.\n[patient] okay. thank you.\n[doctor] you\'re welcome. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Reference Answer:\n[doctor] alright teresa i see here in your chart that you seem to be experiencing some elbow pain could you tell me where it hurts\n[patient] yeah so it\'s hurting on the inside of my elbow\n[doctor] mm-hmm\n[patient] and when i i i\'ve been doing some pottery i\'ve been creating you know i have a pottery wheel and i\'ve been i love my pottery and for my son\'s birthday i\'ve been making a a ceramic bowl and i\'m gon na paint it and i have to do some real full decorations but i\'ve really been working on it a lot and my gosh this is hurting and i ca n\'t work on it right now because it\'s hurting so much\n[doctor] i am so sorry so i mean that\'s really cool that you do parttery it\'s something that i\'ve wanted to pick up you know but i do n\'t know that i have those skills yet does the pain radiate down your arm or up your