ng to get back into it\n[doctor] okay okay well i think it\'s important for you to try to get back into some exercise and to try to avoid foods that are high in sugar\n[patient] yeah\n[doctor] okay okay and i\'m going to order the hemoglobin a1c and i\'m going to continue you on the metformin and i want you to continue to check your blood sugar every morning and log it and i want you to try to get some exercise and avoid foods that are high in sugar\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] okay okay so for your low back pain i\'m going to order an x-ray and i\'m going to refer you to physical therapy and i\'m going to give you a prescription for flexeril and i\'m going to give you some ibuprofen and some tylenol\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] okay and i want you to take the ibuprofen up to three times a day and the tylenol if you need it for severe pain\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] okay and i want you to be careful with the muscle relaxers if you\'re doing any strenuous or hazardous activities like driving\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] okay okay and i\'m going to give you a prescription for the flexeril and i\'m going to order the x-ray so i\'m going to have my nurse come in and help you with that\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] okay so do you have any questions for me\n[patient] no\n[doctor] okay okay\n[patient] no\n[doctor] okay\n[patient] no\n[doctor] okay\n[patient] no\n[doctor] okay okay\n[patient] thank you\n[doctor] okay you\'re welcome\n[patient] thank you\n[doctor] okay bye\n[patient] bye }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] hi, how are you?\n[patient] i\'m doing good.\n[doctor] hey, how can i help you?\n[patient] i\'m having some back pain.\n[doctor] okay. when did it start?\n[patient] about a week ago.\n[doctor] okay. and where is the pain?\n[patient] my back.\n[doctor] okay. and how would you describe the pain?\n[patient] it\'s like a dull ache. it\'s like it\'s in the middle of my back.\n[doctor] okay. and does it radiate to anywhere else?\n[patient] no, it\'s just in the middle of my back.\n[doctor] okay. and how would you rate the pain on a scale of one to ten?\n[patient] i would say a six or a seven.\n[doctor] okay. and have you noticed anything that makes it better or worse?\n[patient] um, it\'s kind of worse when i move, when i move around.\n[doctor] okay. okay. and any other symptoms?\n[patient] i don\'t know, i just feel like i\'m getting a little bit older.\n[doctor] okay. and what do you mean by that?\n[patient] i just feel like i\'m getting a little bit older.\n[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any numbness or tingling in your feet?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. any weakness in your legs?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. any other symptoms?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any medical problems?\n[patient] i have diabetes.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any other medical problems?\n[patient] i have diabetes.\n[doctor] okay. and are you taking any medications?\n[patient] i\'m taking metformin.\n[doctor] okay. and do you take it twice a day?\n[patient] yes.\n[doctor] okay. and do you take it once in the morning and once at night?\n[patient] yes.\n[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any other problems?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any allergies?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and any surgeries?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any other medical problems?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have a family history of diabetes?\n[patient] yes.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have a family history of other medical problems?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and do you smoke?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and do you use alcohol?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and do you use recreational drugs?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and do you work?\n[patient] yes. i work in a bakery.\n[doctor] okay. and how long have you been working there?\n[patient] for about twenty years.\n[doctor] okay. and what kind of things do you do there?\n[patient] i bake and i sell.\n[doctor] okay. okay. and have you noticed anything that you think is related to your back pain?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any other medical problems?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. all right. well, let\'s do a quick physical exam. so, i\'m just going to check your vital signs. your blood pressure is one twenty over seventy. your heart rate is seventy.\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] your respiratory rate is sixteen. your heart exam is normal. your lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. your abdomen is nontender to palpation. your neurological exam is intact. your reflexes are normal. your gait is normal. i\'m just going to do a quick musculoskeletal exam. i\'m just going to check your back. so, your back exam is normal to palpation, except for some pain to palpation of the midline of the lower back, especially on the left. you have some mild straight leg rise on the right. and on the left, you have some positive straight leg rise. and your lower extremities are normal to exam. and your eyes, ears, nose, mouth, and throat exam is normal. all right. so, i\'m gon na go ahead and order a low back x-ray. and i\'m gon na order a referral to physical therapy. i\'m gon na prescribe you four hundred milligrams of ibuprofen up to three times a day. you can take tylenol if you need something for severe pain. i\'m also gon na prescribe you some flexeril. and i\'m gon na have you follow up with me in a week. and i\'m gon na also order a hemoglobin a1c, since you haven\'t had one in almost five months. you\'re gon na continue with your diet and exercise. and you can continue on the metformin for the time being. i\'m gon na have you check your blood sugar in the morning and log that for me. do you have any questions for me?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. all right. is there anything else i can do for you?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. all right. i\'ll see you in a week. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Reference Answer:\n[doctor] good morning noah tell me a little bit about why you are here today\n[patient] hi 