ch does not impact his knee pain. He adds that he is able to perform a full squat without pain. The patient reports numbness and tingling in his right foot, however this is not new. The patient has been taking ibuprofen, which provides him with relief at night. He has also been icing his knee 4 times per day, which provides him with relief in the morning and at the end of the day.\n\nMEDICAL HISTORY\n\nHe states that he has fractured his 2nd toe 3 times over the last 10 years.\n\nSOCIAL HISTORY\n\nThe patient works in sales. He rides a bike for exercise.\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n\nNeurological: Positive for numbness and tingling in his toes on his right foot from prior injury.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAM\n\nCV: >Palpable dorsalis pedis and posterior tibialis pulse.\nMSK: Examination of the right knee: Slight edema. Slight effusion. No pain with palpation of the right lateral knee. Positive varus test. Full ROM. Negative Lachman\'s.\n\nRESULTS\n\n4 views of the right knee were taken. These reveal no evidence of any fractures, dislocations, or bony abnormality. No other abnormalities are noted.\n\nASSESSMENT\n\nRight knee lateral collateral ligament strain.\n\nPLAN\n\nAfter reviewing the patient\'s examination and radiographic findings today, I have had a lengthy discussion with the patient in regards to his current symptoms. I have explained to him that his x-rays did not reveal any acute fractures or bony abnormality. I have recommended that we treat the patient conservatively with formal physical therapy to strengthen his right knee. I have also prescribed the patient meloxicam 15 mg to treat his pain. If his pain does not improve with physical therapy, I will recommend obtaining an MRI.\n\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] Hi, how are you doing today?\n[patient] I\'m doing okay. I\'ve been having some problems with my knee.\n[doctor] Okay. So, what\'s going on with your knee?\n[patient] I stepped off a curb and twisted my ankle about two and a half weeks ago.\n[doctor] Okay. And where exactly is the pain?\n[patient] It\'s on the outside of my right knee.\n[doctor] Alright. And is it painful when you walk?\n[patient] No, it\'s not painful when I walk, unless I stand on one foot for a long time.\n[doctor] Okay. How about when you stand on both feet?\n[patient] No, it\'s not painful when I stand on both feet.\n[doctor] Alright. What about when you stand on your heel?\n[patient] Yes, that\'s when I feel the pain.\n[doctor] Okay. Have you noticed any clicking?\n[patient] Yes, I have been clicking with every step.\n[doctor] Alright. Does it hurt when you bend your knee?\n[patient] No, I can bend all the way down.\n[doctor] Okay. What about when you stand for a long time?\n[patient] It locks up.\n[doctor] Alright. Have you noticed any numbness or tingling?\n[patient] Yes, I\'ve had numbness and tingling in my foot before, but this is not new.\n[doctor] Okay. Have you tried any treatments for the pain?\n[patient] Yes, I\'ve been taking ibuprofen and icing it.\n[doctor] Alright. How has that been helping?\n[patient] It helps at night and in the morning.\n[doctor] Okay. How about in the evening?\n[patient] It helps in the evening as well.\n[doctor] Alright. Do you take any other medications?\n[patient] No, just ibuprofen.\n[doctor] Alright. Do you do any exercises?\n[patient] I bike for exercise.\n[doctor] Okay. How about your job?\n[patient] I\'m in sales.\n[doctor] Alright. Any other problems?\n[patient] No, just my knee.\n[doctor] Okay. So, let me go ahead and check your knee.\n[patient] Okay.\n[doctor] Alright, so on physical exam, I do appreciate some edema and a slight effusion in the right knee. I don\'t appreciate any pain with palpation of the right lateral knee, but I do appreciate a positive varus test. I\'m going to go ahead and check the neurovascular status of your right lower extremity. I do appreciate a palpable dorsalis pedis and posterior tibialis pulse. Now, I\'m going to check the range of motion of your right knee. I\'m going to bend it, straighten it, and rotate it. Everything looks good. I\'m going to check for any pain with a Lachman\'s test. That was negative. Now, I\'m going to go ahead and review the x-rays of your right knee. The x-rays did not reveal any fractures, dislocations, or bony abnormalities. No other abnormalities were noted. Based on your examination and radiographic findings today, I think you have a right knee lateral collateral ligament strain. I\'m going to go ahead and prescribe you meloxicam 15 milligrams to help with your pain. I\'m also going to recommend that we do some formal physical therapy to strengthen your right knee. If your pain does not improve with physical therapy, I will recommend that we get an MRI. Do you have any questions?\n[patient] No, I think that sounds good.\n[doctor] Alright. We will get you set up with physical therapy and get you started with the meloxicam. Do you have any other questions?\n[patient] No, I think that\'s it.\n[doctor] Alright. Thank you, and I\'ll see you in a few weeks.\n[patient] Thank you. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] good morning, gregory. how are you today?\n[patient] i\'m doing okay.\n[doctor] good to see you. i\'m doctor jason from med express. how can i help you today?\n[patient] i have a knee injury. i\'m having some pain in my right knee. i\'ve been having some issues with it for a little over two weeks now. i was walking down the street, and i stepped off the curb and twisted my ankle. i\'ve been having some pain on the lateral side of my knee. i\'ve also been having some clicking, and some pain with ambulation. i\'ve been having some pain when i\'m standing on one foot for a long time. i\'ve also had some pain when i\'m standing, but i have to stand on my heel. i\'ve been having some pain when i\'m resting my foot on my heel. i have not had any pain at rest or elevated, or when my foot is flat on the ground. i\'ve been more active during the day, but it does not impact my knee pain. i\'ve been able to perform a full squat without pain. i\'ve been having some numbness and tingling in my right foot, but that\'s not new. i\'ve been taking ibuprofen, which has given me relief at night. i\'ve also been icing my knee four times a day, which has given me relief in the morning and at the end of the day.\n[doctor] okay. have you had any other injuries in the past?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. any other medical problems?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. have you ever broken a bone?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. have you ever had any surgeries?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. do you have any other medical problems?\n[patient] i have high blood pressure.\n[doctor] okay. and how is that being treated?\n[patient] i\'m taking some medication.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any allergies?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. any other medical problems?\n[patient] i have a history of gout.\n[doctor] okay. and how is that being treated?\n[patient] i take allopurinol.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any allergies?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and how about your medications?\n[patient] i\'m taking a lot of medications.\n[doctor] okay. any other medical problems?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any other medical problems?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and have you ever had any surgeries?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. have you ever broken a bone?\n[patient] yes.\n[patient] i have fractured my second toe three times over the last ten years.\n[doctor] okay. and how is your pain today?\n[patient] it\'s been getting a little better, but i\'m still having some pain.\n[doctor] okay. have you noticed any numbness or tingling in your toes?\n[patient] yes. i\'ve been having some numbness and tingling in my right foot, but that\'s not new.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any other symptoms?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any clicking or catching?\n[patient] yes. i\'ve been having some clicking.\n[doctor] okay. and have you n