 patient reports that she works on a keyboard all day.\n\nMEDICATIONS\n\nThe patient reports that she has been taking ibuprofen.\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n\nConstitutional: Denies sleep disturbance.\nMusculoskeletal: Reports pain in the 1st, 2nd, and 3rd digits on the right hand.\nNeurological: Reports numbness and tingling in the 1st, 2nd, and 3rd digits on the right hand.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAM\n\nMSK: Examination of the right hand: Pain with flexion and extension of the wrist.. Decreased grip strength on the right compared to the left. Positive Tinel\'s sign.\n\nASSESSMENT\n\nRight carpal tunnel syndrome.\n\nPLAN\n\nAfter reviewing her symptoms and exam findings, I believe her symptoms are secondary to carpal tunnel syndrome. We discussed the nature of this condition, as well as her treatment options, in detail. I recommend we treat this conservatively with nighttime wrist splinting and ibuprofen, but I want to increase her dose to 600 mg 4 times daily. I\'m also going to order an EMG/Nerve conduction study for further evaluation. If this is positive, we can consider additional treatment with physical therapy or surgical intervention with carpal tunnel release.\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] okay, so alexis, it\'s nice to see you here today. i understand that you\'ve been having some issues with your right hand. can you tell me a little bit more about what\'s going on?\n[patient] sure. i\'ve been having a lot of pain in my right hand. i\'m a keyboard operator, so i\'m on the computer all day long. i\'ve been having some numbness and tingling in my fingers, and it\'s been getting worse over the past month or so. i\'ve been trying to take it easy and take ibuprofen, but it\'s really been bothering me.\n[doctor] okay. have you noticed any sleep disturbances?\n[patient] no, no sleep disturbances.\n[doctor] okay. okay, so it sounds like it\'s really affecting your daily activities. is that correct?\n[patient] yeah, i\'m always on the keyboard, so it\'s really been affecting me.\n[doctor] okay. okay. have you noticed any pain or numbness in your fingers?\n[patient] yeah, definitely in my first, second and third fingers on my right hand.\n[doctor] okay. okay, have you tried to rest your hand or stop typing?\n[patient] yeah, i\'ve tried resting it and taking ibuprofen, but it\'s really been bothering me.\n[doctor] okay. okay. have you tried any other treatments?\n[patient] no, just ibuprofen.\n[doctor] okay. okay. have you noticed any pain or numbness in your wrist?\n[patient] yes, i do feel pain in my wrist. it\'s been getting worse.\n[doctor] okay. okay. have you tried using a wrist splint?\n[patient] no, i haven\'t.\n[doctor] okay. okay. so let\'s take a look at your hand. i\'m gon na check your wrist and fingers. okay?\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. so i\'m gon na press here on the nerve. does this hurt?\n[patient] yeah, it does.\n[doctor] okay. okay. and then i\'m gon na press here on the nerve. does this hurt?\n[patient] yeah, it does.\n[doctor] okay. okay. so let\'s take a look at your grip strength. okay? so i\'m gon na have you squeeze my hand. okay?\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. and i\'m gon na squeeze back. okay? so i\'m gon na squeeze your hand. okay?\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. and then i\'m gon na release. okay? and then i\'m gon na squeeze your hand again. okay?\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. and i\'m gon na release. okay? so i\'m gon na squeeze your hand. okay? and then i\'m gon na release. okay? so i\'m gon na squeeze your hand. okay? and then i\'m gon na release. okay? so your grip strength is a little bit weaker on the right compared to the left. okay?\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. okay. and then i\'m gon na press here on your wrist. does this hurt?\n[patient] yeah, it does.\n[doctor] okay. okay. so i\'m gon na check for a positive tine\'s sign. okay? so i\'m gon na press here on your wrist. okay? and i\'m gon na hold it. okay? and i\'m gon na release. okay? so i\'m gon na pr