after that, you should be fine to continue playing normally.\n[patient] okay, that sounds good.\n[doctor] you\'re doing well with your diet and your blood pressure is well controlled. let\'s continue with the lisinopril 20 mg a day. we\'ll order a hemoglobin a1c to check if you need any medication adjustments. do you have any other questions?\n[patient] no, i think you covered everything.\n[doctor] okay. well, i\'m going to go ahead and order that hemoglobin a1c. we\'ll see you back in two months for a follow-up. is there anything else you need?\n[patient] no, i think i\'m good.\n[doctor] okay. take care. see you in two months.\n[patient] alright. thank you.\n[doctor] thank you. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] hi, how are you?\n[patient] i\'m doing alright. i\'ve been having some elbow pain.\n[doctor] okay. so what happened?\n[patient] um, my son was playing lacrosse and he hit me with the stick.\n[doctor] okay. so, you\'re a lacrosse player too?\n[patient] yeah. i\'m a lacrosse coach.\n[doctor] okay. so, what position do you play?\n[patient] i\'m the goalie.\n[doctor] okay. and your son, he\'s a field player?\n[patient] yeah. he\'s a midfielder.\n[doctor] okay. so, how did you get hurt?\n[patient] so, he swung the stick and hit me right in the elbow. i\'m pretty sure he\'s trying to get me out of the game.\n[doctor] okay. did you get hurt again?\n[patient] yeah, i got hit a couple times.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, have you been able to play since then?\n[patient] no, i haven\'t been able to play since then.\n[doctor] okay. and, have you been able to move your arm around? how\'s that?\n[patient] it\'s pretty sore. i can move it a little bit.\n[doctor] okay. and, have you been able to straighten it out?\n[patient] yeah, it\'s a little bit sore when i straighten it out.\n[doctor] okay. and, have you been able to bend it?\n[patient] yeah, it\'s a little bit sore when i bend it.\n[doctor] okay. and, have you been able to move it around?\n[patient] yeah, it\'s 