il your elbow heals. after that, you should be fine to continue playing normally. and, i\'m going to prescribe you ibuprofen 800 milligrams twice a day to help with some of the pain and swelling. you should also ice the area in 20-minute intervals 3 times a day to further reduce your symptoms.\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. um, my assessment for your hypertension is as follows : your medical reasoning is that this appears to be well-controlled with dietary modifications and lisinopril. your patient education and counseling is as follows : i encourage you to keep up with your dietary modifications. and, your medical treatment is as follows : we will keep you on lisinopril 20 milligrams a day.\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. and, my assessment for your diabetes is as follows : your medical reasoning is that this appears to be well-controlled at this time. your medical treatment is as follows : we will keep you on metformin 500 milligrams. we will also order a hemoglobin a1c to evaluate any need for medication adjustments.\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. and, um, do you have any questions for me?\n[patient] no, i\'m good.\n[doctor] okay. all right. well, i\'ll see you in a couple of weeks.\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Reference Answer:\n[doctor] hey good to see you philip so i see here you\'re coming in you had some right elbow pain also you have a past medical history of hypertension diabetes we are gon na check up on those as well so can you tell me what happened to your elbow\n[patient] sure i hurt it about a week ago playing lacrosse with my kids just suddenly started hurting me when i was throwing the ball\n[doctor] okay okay so how old are your kids\n[patient] my oldest is thirteen and the other one is ten i was playing with a thirteen -year-old\n[doctor] okay yeah i know i i play with my kids sometimes and i think i\'m getting too old to do all that so i just i\'ve hurt myself before as well alright so with your your elbow what part of